+ * ignored the ECMA-262 9.5.9 [[Set]] `receiver` argument and wrote through to the
+ * host object. A sandbox-side child built via `Object.create(hostObj)` — or a
+ * forged `Reflect.set(hostObj, k, v, customReceiver)` — therefore became a write
+ * channel onto the host object. The fix installs the property on `receiver`
+ * instead when `receiver` is not the canonical bridge proxy for the host object.
